{"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations\/Item\/arpeggiate(_:)"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotations\/item\/arpeggiate(_:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"arpeggiate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" alternative.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations\/Item"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Case","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLNotationsV4ItemO10arpeggiateyAeA13MXLArpeggiateVcAEmF","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"symbolKind":"case","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"arpeggiate","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV","text":"MXLArpeggiate","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"title":"MXLNotations.Item.arpeggiate(_:)"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"arpeggiate","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV","text":"MXLArpeggiate","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLArpeggiate"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLArpeggiate"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The arpeggiate type indicates that this note is part of an arpeggiated chord. The number attribute can be used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to distinguish between two simultaneous chords arpeggiated separately (different numbers) or together (same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number). The direction attribute is used if there is an arrow on the arpeggio sign. By default, arpeggios go"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the lowest to highest note. The length of the sign can be determined from the position attributes for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arpeggiate elements used with the top and bottom notes of the arpeggiated chord. If the unbroken attribute is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set to yes, it indicates that the arpeggio continues onto another staff within the part. This serves as a hint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to applications and is not required for cross-staff arpeggios."}],"title":"MXLArpeggiate"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNotations/Item":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations\/Item","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"One of the alternatives for Notations.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotations\/item","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"MXLNotations.Item","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Item","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Item","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNotations":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotations","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Notations refer to musical notations, not XML notations. Multiple notations are allowed in order to represent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"multiple editorial levels. The print-object attribute, added in Version 3.0, allows notations to represent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"details of performance technique, such as fingerings, without having them appear in the score."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNotations"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNotations"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations","title":"MXLNotations"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNotations/Item/arpeggiate(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotations\/item\/arpeggiate(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations\/Item\/arpeggiate(_:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"arpeggiate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" alternative.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"arpeggiate"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLArpeggiate","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"title":"MXLNotations.Item.arpeggiate(_:)"}}}